{"seconds": 114.6, "exit": 0, "final": "After Bxg5, Black plays Nxg5 and trades pieces. That doesn't win material.\n\nSo Qg4 is definitely the best move. It wins the bishop by force. The main point is that after forcing Black's knights to check, White's queen can capture them while the bishop remains hanging.\n\nNow for the motif and explanation:\n\n**Motif**: The key tactical motif here is \"attraction\" or \"deflection\". The queen move to g4 forces Black's knights to check (attracted to g3 or f2), allowing the queen to capture with the other material still hanging.\n\nActually, I think a better way to describe this is that the bishop on g5 becomes a \"hanging piece\" that Black cannot defend when forced to create counterplay with the knight checks.\n\nLet me write the coaching note now:\n\n---\n\n**Best move**: Qg4\n\n**Main line**: 1.Qg4 Ng3+ (or 1...Nxf2+ 2.Qxf2) 2.Qxg3 and the bishop hangs next move.\n\n**Motif**: hanging piece (or attraction)\n\n**Coaching Note (80 words max)**:\nWhen your opponent creates threats, look for forcing moves that still win material. Here, the Black bishop on g5 is loose (attacked twice, defended once). By playing Qg4, you attack it directly while leaving Black no good options. Black's knights must check (Ng3+ or Nxf2+) to create counterplay, but you capture with the queen and still win the bishop. Always ask: \"Can I threaten their piece while forcing their reply?\"\n\n---\n\nLet me verify the line one more time to make sure it's correct:\n\nPosition after Qg4 (move 1 for White):\n- Queen on g4 attacks bishop on g5\n- Bishop on g5 attacked by queen on g4 and bishop on c1\n- Black knights on e4 and d5\n\nBlack's most forcing response: 1...Ng3+\n\nPosition after Ng3+ (move 1 for Black):\n- Knight on g3 checks king on h1\n- White must respond to check\n\nWhite's best response: 2.Qxg3 (capturing the knight)\n\nPosition after Qxg3 (move 2 for White):\n- Queen on g3 attacks bishop on g5\n- Bishop on g5 is still hanging\n- White is up material (won the knight for nothing)\n\nThis is the correct analysis. The answer is Qg4.\n\n```json\n{\"move\": \"Qg4\", \"line\": [\"Qg4\", \"Ng3+\", \"Qxg3\"], \"motifs\": [\"hangingPiece\"]}\n```", "tool_calls": [{"tool": "skill", "args": {"skill": "chess-coach"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-board", "args": {"fen": "r1b1qrk1/1p5p/p1p1p3/2PnNpb1/1P1Pn3/P4Q2/4BPPP/R1BR3K w - - 0 24"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-threats", "args": {"fen": "r1b1qrk1/1p5p/p1p1p3/2PnNpb1/1P1Pn3/P4Q2/4BPPP/R1BR3K w - - 0 24"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-legal_moves", "args": {"fen": "r1b1qrk1/1p5p/p1p1p3/2PnNpb1/1P1Pn3/P4Q2/4BPPP/R1BR3K w - - 0 24"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r1b1qrk1/1p5p/p1p1p3/2PnNpb1/1P1Pn3/P4Q2/4BPPP/R1BR3K w - - 0 24", "move": "Nf7"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r1b1qrk1/1p5p/p1p1p3/2PnNpb1/1P1Pn3/P4Q2/4BPPP/R1BR3K w - - 0 24", "move": "Ng6"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r1b1qrk1/1p5p/p1p1p3/2PnNpb1/1P1Pn3/P4Q2/4BPPP/R1BR3K w - - 0 24", "move": "Qh5"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r1b1qrk1/1p5p/p1p1p3/2PnNpb1/1P1Pn3/P4Q2/4BPPP/R1BR3K w - - 0 24", "move": "Ng4"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r1b1qrk1/1p5p/p1p1p3/2PnNpb1/1P1Pn3/P4Q2/4BPPP/R1BR3K w - - 0 24", "move": "Nxc6"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r1b1qrk1/1p5p/p1p1p3/2PnNpb1/1P1Pn3/P4Q2/4BPPP/R1BR3K w - - 0 24", "move": "Nd7"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r1b1qrk1/1p5p/p1p1p3/2PnNpb1/1P1Pn3/P4Q2/4BPPP/R1BR3K w - - 0 24", "move": "Nd3"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r1b1qrk1/1p5p/p1p1p3/2PnNpb1/1P1Pn3/P4Q2/4BPPP/R1BR3K w - - 0 24", "move": "Nc4"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r1b1qrk1/1p5p/p1p1p3/2PnNpb1/1P1Pn3/P4Q2/4BPPP/R1BR3K w - - 0 24", "move": "Qh5"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r1b1qrk1/1p5p/p1p1p3/2PnNpb1/1P1Pn1Q1/P7/4BPPP/R1BR3K b - - 1 24", "move": "Nxf2+"}}, {"too